Measured: 13:19:57 the Teach page sent teachGo btnGoOutSht2Right with params.speed 65 (speedEvent), the move ran at 1 %. Golden
GoButton140Click (uteach.cpp:3429-3430) does SetSpeed(ScrollBar1) and then UpdateMotorTeachMonitor, which puts ScrollBar1 at 1 and
SetSpeed(1), so the GO runs at 1 %; GoButton020Click forces 20 then UpdateMotorTeachTwoMonitor (bar to 1) and moves at 20 %. The port
copied both. All Teach GO buttons go through these two handlers (DoTeachButton: kTkGo140 / kTkGo020).

WebMotorAccess.cpp (same lines): TeachGoPct(r) = params.speed clamped 1..100 (as golden edtSpeedChange), else the last speed the page
reported, else 1; TeachGo140 / TeachGo020 set the moving axis to it (TeachSpeedSet) and move at it; the TeachMonitor / TeachTwoMonitor
resets and the forced 20 are gone. Motor Test's GO (DoMoveAbsolute) already used the page speed; Teach Move+/-/MoveTo use the page's
last reported speed -- unchanged.
tests/test_web_motor_access.cpp: + GoButton140 at the page's 65 % -> velHigh 6500; the GoButton020 checks now carry speed 35 and expect
35 % (were golden's 20 %). WebMotorAccess 1104/0. wb_serve compiled; the link waits for EastSun's running program. Scan 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
